G2106.b:
† ⟪εὐ-δοκέω⟫, -ῶ
(on the derivation, v. BL, § 28, 6) [in LXX chiefly for ⁨רָצָה⁩, also for ⁨אָבָה⁩, ⁨חָפֵץ⁩, etc. ;]
⟪1.⟫ c. inf. (Polyb., al.), ⟪to be well pleased, to think it good, to give consent⟫ (so freq. in π. in legal docu­ments; Milligan, Th., 22 f.): ⟦Luke 12:32|Lk 12:32⟧, ⟦Romans 15:26|Ro 15:26-27⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:21|I Co 1:21⟧, ⟦Galatians 1:15|Ga 1:15⟧, ⟦Colossians 1:19|Col 1:19⟧, R, mg. (ICC, in l., but v. infr.), ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:8|I Th 2:8⟧ ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:1|3:1⟧; μᾶλλον εὐ., ⟦2 Corinthians 5:8|II Co 5:8⟧; c. acc et inf. (Polyb., i, 8, 4), ⟦Colossians 1:19|Col, l.c.⟧, R, txt. (Lft., in l).
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to be well pleased⟫ or ⟪take pleasure⟫ with or in a person or thing;
⟪(a)⟫ c. dat. (Polyb., al.; I Mac 1:43, I Es 4:39): ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:12|II Th 2:12⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ as freq. in LXX,
⟪(α)⟫ c. acc: ⟦Matthew 12:13|Mt 12:13⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:5|He 10:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:8|8⟧ (LXX);
⟪β⟫ seq. ἐν (cf. Heb. ⁨רָצָה בְּ⁩, ⟦Psalms 149:4|Ps 149:4⟧): ⟦Matthew 3:17|Mt 3:17⟧ ⟦Matthew 17:5|17:5⟧, ⟦Mark 1:11|Mk 1:11⟧, ⟦Luke 3:22|Lk 3:22⟧ (on the tense, v. M, Pr., 134 f.; DCG, i,308 b), ⟦1 Corinthians 10:5|I Co 10:5⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:10|II Co 12:10⟧, ⟦Hebrews 10:38|He 10:38⟧ (LXX);
⟪(c)⟫ seq. εἰς: ⟦2 Peter 1:17|II Pe 1:17⟧. (cf. συν-ευδοκέω, and v. Cremer, 213 f.; Field, Notes, 48 f.; DCG, i, 355a.)†

G2128.b:
† ⟪εὐλογητός⟫, -όν
(< εὐλογέω), [in LXX chiefly for ⁨בָּרוּךְ⁩ ;] ⟪blessed⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of men (⟦Genesis 12:2|Ge 12:2⟧ A, ⟦Deuteronomy 7:14|De 7:14⟧, ⟦Judges 17:2|Jg 17:2⟧ B, ⟦Ruth 2:20|Ru 2:20⟧, ⟦1 Samuel 15:13|I Ki 15:13⟧);
⟪(b)⟫ of God (Lft., Notes, 310 f.), as chiefly in LXX (⟦Genesis 9:26|Ge 9:26⟧, ⟦Exodus 17:10|Ex 17:10⟧, ⟦Psalms 18:46|Ps 17 (18):46⟧, al.): ⟦Luke 1:68|Lk 1:68⟧, ⟦Romans 1:25|Ro 1:25⟧ ⟦Romans 9:5|9:5⟧ (ICC, in l), ⟦2 Corinthians 1:3|II Co 1:3⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 11:31|11:31⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:3|Eph 1:3⟧, ⟦1 Peter 1:3|I Pe 1:3⟧; absol., ὁ εὐλογητός (Dalman, Words, 200; JThS, v, 453), ⟦Mark 14:61|Mk 14:61⟧ (Cremer, 769).†

G2186.b:
⟪ἐφ-ίστημι⟫
[in LXX for ⁨נָצַב⁩ ni., ⁨שִׁית⁩, ⁨נָתַן⁩, etc. ;]
⟪1.⟫ causal in pres., impf., fut., 1 aor., ⟪to set upon⟫ or ⟪by, set up⟫, etc. (Æsch., Hdt., Arist., al).
⟪2.⟫ Intrans. in mid, and in pf. and 2 aor. act.;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to stand upon⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to be set over⟫;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪to stand by, be present, be at hand, come on⟫ or ⟪upon⟫: ⟦Luke 2:38|Lk 2:38⟧ ⟦Luke 10:40|10:40⟧ ⟦Luke 20:1|20:1⟧, ⟦Acts 6:12|Ac 6:12⟧ ⟦Acts 12:7|12:7⟧ ⟦Acts 22:13|22:13⟧, ⟦Acts 22:20|20⟧ ⟦Acts 23:27|23:27⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 4:2|II Ti 4:2⟧; c. dat. pers., ⟦Luke 2:9|Lk 2:9⟧ ⟦Luke 24:4|24:4⟧, ⟦Acts 4:1|Ac 4:1⟧ ⟦Acts 23:11|23:11⟧; c. dat. loc., ⟦Acts 17:5|Ac 17:5⟧; seq. έπί, c. acc, ⟦Acts 10:17|Ac 10:17⟧ ⟦Acts 11:11|11:11⟧; of rain, ⟦Acts 28:2|Ac 28:2⟧; of evils impending, c. dat. pers., ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:3|I Th 5:3⟧; seq. έπί (Wi 6:9), ⟦Luke 21:34|Lk 21:34⟧; of time, ⟦2 Timothy 4:6|II Ti 4:6⟧ (cf. κατ-, συν-εφίστημι).†

G2192.b:
⟪ἔχω⟫,
[in LXX for ⁨אָצֵל⁩ (ἐχόμενος), ⁨בַּעַל⁩, ⁨יֵשׁ⁩, etc., 59 words in all;] (on the Aktionsart of the various tenses, v. M, Pr., 110, 145, 150, 183), ⟪to have⟫, as in cl., in various senses and constructions.
⟪I.⟫ Trans.;
	⟪1.⟫ ⟪to have⟫, ⟪hold⟫, ⟪hold fast⟫, etc.;
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to hold⟫, as, in the hand: ⟦Revelation 5:8|Re 5:8⟧ ⟦Revelation 14:6|14:6⟧, al.; ἐν τ. χειρί, ⟦Revelation 1:16|Re 1:16⟧ ⟦Revelation 10:2|10:2⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ of arms and clothing, = φέρω, φορέω, ⟪to bear⟫, ⟪wear⟫: ⟦Matthew 3:4|Mt 3:4⟧ ⟦Matthew 22:12|22:12⟧, al.; so freq. pres. ptcp. (LS, s.v., A, I, 6; Bl., § 74, 2), ⟦Mark 11:13|Mk 11:13⟧, ⟦John 18:10|Jo 18:10⟧, ⟦Revelation 9:17|Re 9:17⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ of a woman, ἐν γαστρὶ ἔ (κοίτην ἔ.), ⟪to be with child⟫: ⟦Mark 13:17|Mk 13:17⟧, ⟦Romans 9:10|Ro 9:10⟧;
		⟪(d)⟫ ⟪to hold fast⟫, ⟪keep⟫: ⟦Luke 19:20|Lk 19:20⟧; metaph., of the mind and conduct, ⟦Mark 16:8|Mk 16:8⟧ (cf. ⟦Job 21:6|Jb 21:6⟧, ⟦Isaiah 13:8|Is 13:8⟧; Deiss., BS, 293; Field, Notes, 44 f.), ⟦John 14:21|Jo 14:21⟧, ⟦Romans 1:28|Ro 1:28⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 3:9|I Ti 3:9⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:13|II Ti 1:13⟧, ⟦Revelation 6:9|Re 6:9⟧, al.;
		⟪(e)⟫ ⟪to involve⟫: ⟦Hebrews 10:35|He 10:35⟧(LXX), ⟦James 1:4|Ja 1:4⟧, ⟦John 4:18|I Jo 4:18⟧;
		⟪(f)⟫ = Lat. habere (Bl., § 34, 5; 73, 5), ⟪to hold⟫, ⟪consider⟫: c. acc. et predic. ptcp., ⟦Luke 14:18|Lk 14:18⟧; c. acc., seq. ὡς, ⟦Matthew 14:5|Mt 14:5⟧; εἰς (Hebraism), ⟦Matthew 21:46|Mt 21:46⟧; on (Bl., § 70, 2), ⟦Mark 11:32|Mk 11:32⟧.
	⟪2.⟫ ⟪to have⟫, ⟪possess⟫;
		⟪(a)⟫ in general, c. acc. rei: ⟦Matthew 19:22|Mt 19:22⟧, ⟦Mark 10:22|Mk 10:22⟧, ⟦Luke 12:19|Lk 12:19⟧, ⟦John 10:16|Jo 10:16⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:22|I Co 11:22⟧, al.; of wealth or poverty, absol., ἔχειν (neg. οὐκ, μή), ⟦Matthew 13:12|Mt 13:12⟧ ⟦Matthew 25:29|25:29⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 8:12|II Co 8:12⟧; ἐκ τ. ἔχειν, ⟪according to your means⟫, ⟦2 Corinthians 8:11|II Co 8:11⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ of relationship, association, etc.: πατέρα, ⟦John 8:41|Jo 8:41⟧; γυναῖκα (MM, xiv), ⟦1 Corinthians 7:2|I Co 7:2⟧; φίλον, ⟦Luke 11:5|Lk 11:5⟧; βασιλέα, ⟦John 19:15|Jo 19:15⟧; ποιμένα, ⟦Matthew 9:36|Mt 9:36⟧; c. dupl. acc., ⟦Matthew 3:9|Mt 3:9⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ of parts or members: ὦτα, ⟦Matthew 19:15|Mt 19:15⟧; μέλη, ⟦Romans 12:4|Ro 12:4⟧; θεμελίους,
		⟪(d)⟫ c. acc., as periphrasis of verb: μνεῖαν ἔ. (= μεμνῆσθαι), ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:6|I Th 3:6⟧; ἀγάπην, ⟦John 13:35|Jo 13:35⟧; γνῶσιν, ⟦1 Corinthians 8:1|I Co 8:1⟧; πεποίθησιν, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:4|II Co 3:4⟧; θλίψιν, ⟦John 16:33|Jo 16:33⟧, etc. (Thayer, s.v., I, 2, f., g.);
		⟪(e)⟫ of duty, necessity, etc.: ἀνάγκην, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:37|I Co 7:37⟧; νόμον, ⟦John 19:7|Jo 19:7⟧; ἐπιταγήν, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:25|I Co 7:25⟧; ἀγῶνα, ⟦Philippians 1:30|Phl 1:30⟧; κρίμα, ⟦1 Timothy 5:12|I Ti 5:12⟧;
		⟪(f)⟫ of complaints and disputes; κατά, c. gen. pers., ⟦Matthew 5:23|Mt 5:23⟧, ⟦Mark 11:25|Mk 11:25⟧; id. seq. ὅτι, ⟦Revelation 2:4|Re 2:4⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:20|20⟧; c. acc. seq. πρός, ⟦Acts 24:19|Ac 24:19⟧, al.;
		⟪(g)⟫ c. inf.,
			⟪(α)⟫ (cl.) ⟪to be able⟫ (Field, Notes, 14): ⟦Matthew 18:25|Mt 18:25⟧, ⟦Mark 14:8|Mk 14:8⟧ (sc. ποιῆσαι), ⟦Luke 12:4|Lk 12:4⟧, ⟦Acts 4:14|Ac 4:14⟧, al;
			⟪(β)⟫ of necessity (Bl., § 69, 4): ⟦Luke 12:50|Lk 12:50⟧, ⟦Acts 23:17|Ac 23:17-19⟧ ⟦Acts 28:19|28:19⟧.
⟪II.⟫ Intrans. (Bl., § 53, 1), ⟪to be⟫ in a certain condition: ἑτοίμως ἔ., c. inf., ⟦Acts 21:13|Ac 21:13⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 12:14|II Co 12:14⟧; ἐσχάτως (q.v.), ⟦Mark 5:23|Mk 5:23⟧; κακῶς, ⟪to be ill⟫, ⟦Matthew 4:24|Mt 4:24⟧, al.; καλῶς, ⟦Mark 16:18|Mk 16:[18]⟧; κομψότερον, ⟦John 4:52|Jo 4:52⟧; πῶς, ⟦Acts 15:36|Ac 15:36⟧; impers., ἄλλως ἔχει, ⟪it is otherwise⟫, ⟦1 Timothy 5:25|I Ti 5:25⟧; οὕτως, ⟦Acts 7:1|Ac 7:1⟧, al.; τὸ νῦν ἔχον, ⟪as things now are⟫ (To 7:11), ⟦Acts 24:25|Ac 24:25⟧.
⟪III.⟫ Mid., -ομαι, ⟪to hold oneself fast⟫, ⟪hold on⟫ or ⟪cling to⟫, ⟪be next to⟫: c. gen., τ. ἐχόμενα σωτηρίας, ⟦Hebrews 6:9|He 6:9⟧ (Rendall, in l.); ptcp., ὁ ἐχόμενος, ⟪near⟫, ⟪next⟫: of place, ⟦Mark 1:38|Mk 1:38⟧; of time, τ. ἐχομένῃ (ἡμέρα, expressed or understood), ⟦Luke 13:33|Lk 13:33⟧, ⟦Acts 20:15|Ac 20:15⟧ ⟦Acts 21:26|21:26⟧; (σαββάτῳ), ⟦Acts 13:44|Ac 13:44⟧. (Cf. ἀν-, προσ-αν-, ἀντ-, ἀπ-, ἐν-, ἐπ-, κατ-, μετ-, παρ-, περι-, προ-, προσ-, συν-, ὑπερ-, ὑπ-έχω.)

G2193.b:
⟪ἕως⟫, relative particle (Lat. donee, usque), expressing the terminus ad quem (cf. Burton, § 321 ff.).
⟪I.⟫ As conjunction;
	⟪1.⟫ ⟪till, until⟫;
		⟪(a)⟫ of a fact in past time, c. indic.: ⟦Matthew 2:9|Mt 2:9⟧, al. (Wi 10:14, al.);
		⟪(b)⟫ ἕως ἄν, c. subjc. aor.: ⟦Matthew 2:13|Mt 2:13⟧ ⟦Matthew 5:18|5:18⟧, ⟦Mark 6:10|Mk 6:10⟧, al.; without ἄν (M. Pr., 168 f.; Lft., Notes, 115), ⟦Mark 14:32|Mk 14:32⟧ (Burton, § 325), ⟦Luke 12:59|Lk 12:59⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 2:7|II Th 2:7⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ c. indic., pres. (Burton, § 328; BL, § 65, 10): ⟦Mark 6:45|Mk 6:45⟧, ⟦John 21:22|Jo 21:22⟧, ⟦John 21:23|23⟧ ⟦1 Timothy 4:13|I Ti 4:13⟧.
	⟪2.⟫ C. indic., ⟪as long as, while⟫ (Burton, § 327): ⟦John 9:4|Jo 9:4⟧ (Plat., Phaedo, 89 c).
⟪II.⟫ As an adverb (chiefly in late writers).
	⟪1.⟫ Of time, ⟪until, unto⟫;
		⟪(a)⟫ as prep. c. gen. (BL, § 40, 6; M, Pr., 99): τ. ἡμέρας, ⟦Matthew 26:29|Mt 26:29⟧, ⟦Luke 1:80|Lk 1:80⟧, ⟦Romans 11:8|Ro 11:8⟧, al.; ὥρας, ⟦Matthew 27:45|Mt 27:45⟧, al.; τέλους, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:8|I Co 1:8⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 1:13|II Co 1:13⟧; τ. νῦν, ⟦Matthew 24:21|Mt 24:21⟧, ⟦Mark 13:19|Mk 13:19⟧ (I Mac 2:33); ἐτῶν ὀγ. (Field, Notes, 49 f.), ⟦Luke 2:37|Lk 2:37⟧; τ. ἐλθεῖν, ⟦Acts 8:40|Ac 8:40⟧; before names and events, ⟦Matthew 1:17|Mt 1:17⟧ ⟦Matthew 2:15|2:15⟧, ⟦Luke 11:51|Lk 11:51⟧, ⟦James 5:7|Ja 5:7⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ seq. οὗ, ὅτου, with the force of a conjc. (Burton, § 330; M, Pr., 91);
			⟪(α)⟫ ἕ. οὗ (Hdt., ii, 143; Plut., al.): c. indic., ⟦Matthew 1:25|Mt 1:25⟧ (WH br., οὗ) ⟦Matthew 13:33|13:33⟧, al.; c. subjc. aor., ⟦Matthew 14:22|Mt 14:22⟧, al.;
			⟪(β)⟫ ἔ. ὅτου: c. subjc., ⟦Luke 13:8|Lk 13:8⟧; c. indic., ⟦Matthew 5:25|Mt 5:25⟧ (⟪until⟫), ⟦John 9:18|Jo 9:18⟧;
		⟪(c)⟫ c. adv. (ἕ. ὀψέ, Thuc., iii, 108): ἄρτι, ⟦Matthew 11:12|Mt 11:12⟧, ⟦John 2:10|Jo 2:10⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:13|I Co 4:13⟧, al.; πότε (M, Pr., 107), ⟦Matthew 17:17|Mt 17:17⟧, ⟦Mark 9:19|Mk 9:19⟧, ⟦John 10:24|Jo 10:24⟧, al.
	⟪2.⟫ Of place, ⟪as far as, even to, unto⟫ (Arist., al.);
		⟪(a)⟫ as prep. c. gen. (v. supr.): ⟦Matthew 11:23|Mt 11:23⟧, ⟦Luke 10:15|Lk 10:15⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ c. adv. (BL, § 40, 6): ἄνω, ⟦John 2:7|Jo 2:7⟧; ἔσω, ⟦Mark 14:54|Mk 14:54⟧; κάτω, ⟦Matthew 27:51|Mt 27:51⟧, ⟦Mark 15:38|Mk 15:38⟧; ὧδε, ⟦Luke 23:5|Lk 23:5⟧;
		⟪(c)⟫ c. prep.: ἔξω, ⟦Acts 21:5|Ac 21:5⟧; πρός, ⟦Luke 24:50|Lk 24:50⟧ (Field, Notes, 83).
	⟪3.⟫ Of quantity, measure, etc.: ⟦Matthew 18:21|Mt 18:21⟧, ⟦Mark 6:23|Mk 6:23⟧, ⟦Luke 22:51|Lk 22:51⟧, al.

G2197.b:
⟪Ζαχαρίας⟫, -ου, ὁ (Heb. ⁨זְכַרְיָה⁩, ⁨זְכַרְיָהוּ⁩);
⟪1.⟫ ⟪Zacharias⟫, father of John the Baptist: ⟦Luke 1:5|Lk 1:5⟧, ⟦Luke 1:12|12⟧, ⟦Luke 1:13|13⟧, ⟦Luke 1:18|18⟧, ⟦Luke 1:21|21⟧, ⟦Luke 1:40|40⟧, ⟦Luke 1:59|59⟧, ⟦Luke 1:67|67⟧ ⟦Luke 3:2|3:2⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪Zechariah⟫, the son of Jehoiada (in txt. wrongly called son of Barachiah; cf. ⟦2 Chronicles 24:19|II Ch 24:19⟧ ff.): ⟦Matthew 23:35|Mt 23:35⟧, ⟦Luke 11:51|Lk 11:51⟧.†
